>Okay, I guess I am missing something here.... How is one supposed to
>identify scrolls and potions if not by reading and quaffing them?

You can determine their blessed/cursed status by dropping them on an 
altar (which is what's being refered to here).  You also know that
automatically if you're a Priest. I normally will quaff potions as
soon as I know they're not cursed.  This can be determined by seeing
if your pet will step on them.  (Pet's don't step on cursed item's, 
unless there is food on them, or sometimes "reluctantly").

I don't think anyone's suggesting never to read a scroll/quaff a potion
until you identify it -- just not until you find out if it's cursed.
(Hopefully obvious point: Identifying an object is a sure way to  
determine what the blessed/cursed status.  This is done by reading a 
scroll/spellbook of identify [or once in a blue moon when you sit on 
a throne]).
